   "source": [
    "# 2. Data Cleaning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "BRFSS uses specific codes for \"Don't know/Not sure\" (usually 7, 77, 777) and \"Refused\" (usually 9, 99, 999). We must thoughtfully map these to `NaN` and standardize valid ranges. Careless deletion could introduce bias, so we convert specific invalid inputs to `NaN` first before dropping incomplete records for our clustering profiles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Handle numeric health codes (88=None, 77/99=NaN)\n",
    "for col in ['Physical_Health_Days', 'Mental_Health_Days']:\n",
    "    df[col] = df[col].replace(88, 0).replace([77, 99], np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Sleep_Hours'] = df['Sleep_Hours'].replace([77, 99], np.nan)\n",
    "df['BMI_Indicator'] = df['BMI_Indicator'] / 100.0\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Mapping every categorical value to numerical values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Map Categorical Strings to Numeric\n",
    "health_map = {'Excellent': 1, 'Very good': 2, 'Good': 3, 'Fair': 4, 'Poor': 5}\n",
    "df['General_Health'] = df['General_Health'].map(health_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "yes_no_map = {'Yes': 1, 'No': 2}\n",
    "for col in ['Depression_Diagnosis', 'Exercise_Any', 'Health_Plan', 'Smoked_100_Cigs']:\n",
    "    df[col] = df[col].map(yes_no_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "income_map = {\n",
    "    'Less than $10,000': 1, 'Less than $15,000': 2, 'Less than $20,000': 3,\n",
    "    'Less than $25,000': 4, 'Less than $35,000': 5, 'Less than $50,000': 6,\n",
    "    'Less than $75,000': 7, '$75,000 or more': 8\n",
    "}\n",
    "df['Income_Level'] = df['Income_Level'].map(income_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "marital_map = {\n",
    "    'Married': 1, 'Divorced': 2, 'Widowed': 3, 'Separated': 4, \n",
    "    'Never married': 5, 'A member of an unmarried couple': 6\n",
    "}\n",
    "df['Marital_Status'] = df['Marital_Status'].map(marital_map)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Force all columns to be Numeric (to fix the ValueError)\n",
    "for col in df.columns:\n",
    "    df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors='coerce')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Alcohol Consumption Data Normalization**\n",
    "\n",
    "To analyze the data, we convert different reporting units into a uniform Days Per Month metric:\n",
    "\n",
    "`Weekly Reports` (101 - 107): These represent 1 to 7 days per week. We subtract 100 and multiply by 4.3 (average weeks per month) to get the monthly total.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: Code 102 = 2 days/week = 8.6 days/month.\n",
    "\n",
    "`Monthly Reports` (201 - 230): These represent 1 to 30 days per month. We simply subtract 200 to get the actual number of days.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: Code 210 = 10 days/month.\n",
    "\n",
    "`Zero Consumption` (888): This code is used when a respondent reports drinking 0 days in the past 30 days.\n",
    "\n",
    "`Excluded Data` (777 / 999): These codes represent \"Don't Know\" or \"Refused\" and are converted to NaN (null) so \n",
    "they don't skew our averages.\n",
    "\n",
    "Goal: This conversion puts everyone on the same scale (0–31 days), making it possible to calculate averages and create visualizations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Process \"Alcohol Days\"\n",
    "def parse_alc(x):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(x): return np.nan\n",
    "    val = float(x)\n",
    "    if val == 888: return 0\n",
    "    if val in [777, 999]: return np.nan\n",
    "    if 101 <= val <= 107: return (val - 100) * 4.3\n",
    "    if 201 <= val <= 230: return val - 200\n",
    "    return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "if 'Alcohol_Days' in df.columns:\n",
    "    df['Alcohol_Days_Monthly'] = df['Alcohol_Days'].apply(parse_alc)\n",
    "    df.drop('Alcohol_Days', axis=1, inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
